      "history_summaries": [
        "Round 1/3: Fixed DUT timing bug where position overshoots the required value in the same cycle a state transition fires. Root cause: position update and state machine transition are both registered and update simultaneously — when position=12 triggers state 0→1, position increments to 13 in the same cycle, causing assertion entry_state1_requires_pos12_up to fail. Fix adds `freezePosition` signal that prevents position from incrementing/decrementing when any entry-transition condition is about to fire (state=0 & pos=12 & upReg, state=1 & pos=21 & downReg, state=2 & pos=15 & upReg). This is a homologous repair: all three structurally identical entry assertions (entry_state1_requires_pos12_up, entry_state2_requires_pos21_down, entry_state3_requires_pos15_up) are fixed by the same mechanism. The exit assertions and liveness property are also expected to benefit because position no longer overshoots during transitions, preserving the intended temporal semantics.",
        "Round 2/3: Fixed assertion timing mismatch in 6 entry/exit assertions. Error type: assertion_error. Root cause: assertions checked upReg/downReg/position at the cycle where prevState/state shows the transition, but these registers had already been updated to new values by that same posedge, losing the snapshot that triggered the transition. Fix: added prevUpReg=RegNext(upReg), prevDownReg=RegNext(downReg), and moved prevPosition=RegNext(position) earlier, then used these registered values (snapshot from cycle before transition) in all 6 entry/exit assertions. All assertion labels preserved exactly. The freezePosition DUT fix from round 1 is retained as it prevents position overshoot during transitions.",
        "Round 3/3: Two fixes applied. (1) DUT bug: removed `when(upReg) { state := 0.U }` in state 1 and `when(downReg) { state := 0.U }` in state 2 — these resets made it structurally impossible to ever reach state 2 or 3 because pressing UP (needed to advance position toward 21) or DOWN (needed to advance position toward 15) immediately reset the state machine to 0. Fix preserves state 3→0 reset on any press. (2) Assertion bug: fixed `position_stable_when_both_pressed` — the old check `position === prevPosition` (where prevPosition=RegNext(position)) falsely failed when position was updated in the previous cycle (single-button press) then both-buttons-pressed in the current cycle, because prevPosition held the stale value from 2 cycles ago. New check directly asserts that neither update condition fires when both buttons are pressed, which is correct by construction of the position update logic. All assertion labels preserved."
      ],
